  "limitations": [
    "Browser sessions use a per-process secret: restart, a second worker process or a WEB_AUTH_TOKEN change requires signing in again.",
    "No sign-out control or server-side revocation; a captured session cookie stays valid until restart, token rotation or 12-hour expiry.",
    "A page on another port of the same host can overwrite the session cookie (sign-out nuisance) but cannot forge one; duplicate cookies fail closed.",
    "Default allowed origin is the listening socket (http://127.0.0.1:5000 by default); localhost aliases, Docker published ports, reverse proxies and Host-derived WSGI servers need WEB_ALLOWED_ORIGINS.",
    "Secure is not inferred behind a TLS-terminating proxy.",
    "Engines that send neither Origin nor Fetch Metadata on cross-site POSTs are classified as non-browser clients.",
    "Read (GET) routes remain unauthenticated and do not validate the Host header (DNS rebinding for reads is open).",
    "No rate limiting on /auth/login."
  ],
